# tsconfig.node.json compiles vite.config.ts as a composite project
# reference without noEmit, so `tsc -b` writes these two files fresh on
# every build — they were accidentally committed at some point, which
# matters because Vite's config-file search checks vite.config.js *before*
# vite.config.ts and uses whichever it finds first, so a committed, stale
# vite.config.js would silently shadow real edits to the .ts source for
# anyone who skips the build step before inspecting it.
vite.config.js
vite.config.d.ts

# Brand source art — not bundled; regenerate assets with scripts/gen-logo.mjs
src/assets/logo-source.png
